K3. "Ring 3 isolation" is in the commit title. No code enters ring 3. The
GDT has no user segments, and the only DPL in the three files is the TSS
at DPL 0. Nothing sets the page-table USER bit, and nothing does iretq or
sysret to CPL 3. Every "process" runs in ring 0, so a separate PML4 does
not isolate it. The "PID 2 isolation" selftest checks can only test the
capability table.

$ grep -nE 'iretq|sysret|RPL|ring ?3|Ring 3|0x1b|0x23|USER_CS|user_cs|DPL' kernel/src/proc.rs kernel/src/sched.rs kernel/src/gdt.rs
